course: dictionary
lesson: 12474
title: Deformity: an unusual or twisted shape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A deformity is a part of the body that has an unusual or twisted shape. It can be there from birth, or it can happen after an illness or an injury. «The doctor said the boy's deformity could be helped with a special operation.» The clues are doctor and operation, so a deformity is a body shape that medicine can sometimes help.
explain: Be kind when you use this word. Many people prefer words like «difference» or «condition» when they talk about a person. A word about someone's body should never be used to make them feel small or left out.
explain: Some old stories wrongly used a deformity to show that a character was evil. That is a myth, not a fact. «The wicked king had a twisted back, so everyone said he was cruel.» A body's shape does not show what a person is like inside.
fact: Deformity is a noun: a deformity, deformities.
fact: A deformity is a part of the body with an unusual or twisted shape.
fact: A deformity can be there from birth, or come after an illness or injury.
fact: Doctors can treat some deformities with operations, special shoes or braces.
fact: Many people prefer words like «difference» or «condition» when they talk about a person.
exercise: «The doctor explained that her deformity was there from birth.» What is a deformity? | A small bird that cannot fly | A loud noise made by a drum | *A part of the body with an unusual or twisted shape | A sort of sweet treat
exercise: What can doctors sometimes do for a deformity? | Make it disappear with a wish | *Use an operation, braces or special shoes | Give it a new name only | Ask the person to hide it
exercise: Which word do many people prefer to use instead of deformity when they talk about a person? | monster | weird | *difference | evil
test: «The old story said the wicked witch had a deformity, so everyone knew she was evil.» What is wrong with this story? | Stories are always true | Witches always have green skin | *A body's shape does not show whether a person is evil | Deformities are always easy to see
test: A deformity can come from | Only a fall from a tree | Only a bad dream | *Birth, or after an illness or injury | Never anything, it is just a rumour
exam: Which sentence uses deformity correctly? | He ran very deformity fast to the shop. | The sunny sky was a deformity. | *The baby was born with a deformity in her hand, and the doctors made a plan to help. | She ate a deformity for lunch.
